      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Interesting idea.\n\nJust for full context, when a user is kicked from an instance, they cannot join back to that instance for a full hour.\n\nThis is however an issue for events lasting longer than an hour or events that move between instances a lot, so this suggestion would help to solve those issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-07-08T15:11:42.127Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Please add an official Temporary Group Ban action for group moderation.\n\nCurrently, group moderators can kick a user from the current instance, or ban them from the group permanently until manually unbanned. There is no built-in way to remove a user for a limited time, such as 30 minutes, 2 hours, or 24 hours.\n\nRequested behavior:\n\n- Moderator selects a ban duration.\n\n- The user is removed from the active group instance immediately.\n\n- The user cannot join group instances owned by that group until the timer expires.\n\n- The ban automatically expires without manual unban.\n\n- The action appears in Group Audit Logs with moderator, reason, duration, expiration time, and target user.\n\nWhy this is useful:\n\nTemporary bans would help communities handle short-term disruptions without using permanent group bans. It would reduce over-moderation, improve fairness, and remove the need for external tools or unsafe client automation to enforce timed moderation.\n\nRelated issue:\n\nGroup bans issued through the website/API currently do not always remove a user from an active group instance:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/real-time-enforcement-issue-with-group-bans-via-website-api\n\nClarification:\n\nIdeally, this should work as a temporary Group Instance restriction, not necessarily as a full removal from group membership.\n\nFor many communities, the goal is to remove a disruptive user from active group instances and prevent them from rejoining group-owned instances for a limited time, without permanently removing them from the group or requiring a manual unban later.\n\nSuggested permission model:\n\nThis could be controlled by a separate group permission, for example “Temporary Instance Ban”, so groups can allow moderators to use timed removals without giving them full permanent group ban permissions.",
